      "content": "Since this injury involves a rusty object, you must thoroughly clean the wound immediately as infection risk is high. Wash the area gently with soap and running water, applying gentle pressure if there is active bleeding. After cleaning, apply an antiseptic solution or ointment before covering it with a sterile bandage. However, because of the deep puncture and rust, you should seek professional medical attention as soon as possible to assess the need for a tetanus shot.",
