      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using hydrogen peroxide or alcohol inside the wound can actually damage the tissue and slow down healing, so avoid drenching it. While you can apply a thick layer of antibiotic ointment, wrapping it too tightly will cut off circulation, which is very dangerous for a foot injury. Instead, use sterile gauze pads to cover the wound and change this dressing periodically throughout your workday to absorb any drainage. Please remember that this is a temporary measure, and professional medical care is essential for this type of wound.",
